 "notes": "Shelf rebuilt into 9 kinds (3 new: Rugby shirt, Breton shirt, Baby bodysuit). Dropped: wholesale blank SKUs (AS Colour, Bella+Canvas, Comfort Colors, Gildan, Next Level), POTRENDS range, Daily Bike Lina/Lino and Hanes Moves tank (obscure/SKU noise), BustedBrand latex bodysuit, LeBram Ventoux (retro cycling jersey → Sports), 16 of 18 Disturbia corset SKUs and most NA-KD/Atsuko Kudo duplicates, Hering duplicate. Saint James models moved into the Breton shirt archetype; J.Crew/generic rugby moved to Rugby shirt; Gerber Onesies moved to Baby bodysuit; generic Baseball/Henley/Tall/Marinière entries became types. Years left 'unknown' where no retrieved page gave them (Champion T1011, Merz 215, Lululemon Align, Petit Bateau marinière, RL rugby); Fred Perry M12 dated 1957 per retrieved source rather than the brief's 1952. Brand founding years blank for Champion, Bonds, Merz, Gerber (not on retrieved pages). Team jersey kept tier/kind-level with line ranges only, no titles. SPARQL backbone query returned empty and was not retried due to budget.",
